 {"q": "How does Jesus' answer in Luke 22 differ most from Plato's picture of the ruler?", "options": ["Jesus says no one should have authority", "Plato's ruler comes down because the law compels him and rules as one who knows; Jesus says the greatest must be like a servant, and himself serves", "Jesus agrees that philosophers should rule", "Plato says rulers should be humble servants of the poor"], "answer": 1, "why": "'One who is governing, as one who serves'. Jesus does not abolish authority, which rules out the first option, but turns it upside down."}
